<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS CUT KEY RATE TO 4.50 PCT.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS CUT KEY RATE TO 4.50 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's independent savings banks said in a statement on Tuesday that their reference rate will be lowered to 4.50 percent from 5.00 percent effective September 11.</p>
<p>The savings banks' reference rate is a weighted calculated avereage of the one-, three- and 12-month Helibor market interest rates and of the three-, five- and 10-year bond yields over 20 days.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
</text>
